  "problem_statement": "feat: opt-in semantic self-heal via real type-checkers\n\nquick_check() only catches syntax errors -- a type mismatch or bad\nreference across files sails through until a full tester round-trip.\nWELLS_SEMANTIC_CHECK=1 runs a project-aware type-checker (pyright/mypy\nfor Python, tsc for TypeScript, cargo check for Rust, go vet for Go)\nafter each write/edit and feeds errors back to the model immediately.\nOff by default and skipped when the fast syntax check already failed,\nsince these run whole-project and take seconds rather than milliseconds.\n\nAlso fixes a Windows-specific bug this surfaced: subprocess.run() can't\nlaunch npm-installed .cmd shims (tsc, etc.) by bare name without\nshell=True -- resolve via shutil.which() first.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
